{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791811067,"nonce":"uR7oQUpLzgSO40A2kmjbO5K8OEM=","title":"Disposing a Tooltip owner while its tooltip is open throws Null access","message":"Reproduced in ChimpMonk WorkspaceSnapshot with current local AshUI: hover a FloatingPanel collapse/expand button for 0.6 seconds, capture the tooltip, then dispose the enclosing Owner.root while the tooltip remains open. Owner.dispose throws Null access at its cleanup invocation (Owner.hx:70). Tooltip label and rendering are correct; moving the pointer away and settling its exit animation before disposal avoids the failure. Tooltip creates its visible content under a child owner, but its parent cleanup calls entry.close after children have already been disposed. TopEntry.close dereferences content.node.id without the null guard used in TopEntry.place, so this is a likely cleanup ordering fault. Check owner teardown with open top-layer content and add a focused regression. ChimpMonk reproducer is editor/tests/WorkspaceSnapshot.hx: remove the final Pointer.move and settle before log.stop, then run scripts/editor.sh --snapshot. Observed with default Ash application preset; no evidence yet of a runtime-specific issue.","files":null}]}